          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJB_LLM_EXTRACT_CONTEXT",
          "id": "1772454824686",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772454824687_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an **information extraction engine**.\n\nCRITICAL REDWOODUI MAPPING RULE:\nFor RedwoodUI path, do not re-extract ProjectNumber, ContractNumber, Status, FromDate, ToDate, or Intent from the user message.\n\nYou must directly copy these fields from Relevancy Checker output:\n\nIF  {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.Relevant == 'Yes'}} AND  {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_CODE_CHECK_SOURCE.$output.result == 'RedwoodUI'}} THEN \n\n## OUTPUT (STRICT)\nReturn **ONLY** valid JSON (no markdown, no extra text) with **exactly** these keys and casing:\n\n{\n  \"ProjectNumber\": String|null,\n  \"ContractNumber\": String|null,\n  \"Status\": String|null,\n  \"FromDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\"|null,\n \"ToDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\"|null,\n  \"NoInput\": Boolean|null,\n  \"TotalProjNum\": Integer|null,\n  \"TotalContNum\": Integer|null,\n  \"Intent\": \"List\"|\"Summarize\"|null,\n  \"ambiguities\": String|null,\n  \"clarifyingQuestions\": String|null,\n  \"NoAmbiguity\": Boolean|null\n}\n\n## Extraction rules\n\n### 1) ProjectNumber \n {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAProject == null ?  $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAOldProject : $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAProject}}\n\n-- Make sure that ProjectNumber is enclosed in single quotes ( ' ' )\nExamples:  'Test Project 12', 'Test_Project_123', 'CDRMPJB_RO Project123' \n\n### 2) ContractNumber \n {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAContract == null ?  $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAOldContract : $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAContract}}\n\n-- Make sure that ContractNumber is enclosed in single quotes ( ' ' )\nExamples:  'Test Contract 12', 'Test_Contract_123', 'CDRMPJB_RO & Bil Title' \n\n### 3) Status \n {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAStatus == null ?  $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAOldStatus  : $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAStatus}}\n\n### 4) FromDate\n {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAFromDate == null ?  $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAOldFromDate : $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAFromDate}}\n\n### 5) ToDate \n {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAToDate == null ?  $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAOldToDate : $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAToDate}}\n\n### 6) NoInput \n False\n\n### 7) TotalProjNum \n Return count of extracted project numbers : \n\n    If none → TotalProjNum = 0\n    Else number of unique extracted ProjectNumbers (after de-duplication)\n     \n### 8)  TotalContNum \n\nReturn count of extracted contract numbers:  \n\n    If none → TotalContNum = 0\n    Else number of unique extracted ContractNumbers (after de-duplication)\n\n### 9) ambiguities\n {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.AmbiguityReasonCode}}\n \n### 10) clarifyingQuestions \n {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.AmbiguityReasonCode}}\n \n\n### 11) NoAmbiguity \n Return  true if there no ambiguities or clarifyingQuestions. Otherwise set it as false.\n\n### 12) Intent\n {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAUserIntention}}\n\n\n\nELSE \n\nINPUTS (verbatim; do not infer anything not present except for FromDate and ToDate): \n\n    userQuestion: {{$context.$variables.prjPjbVarUquserQuestion}}\n    Chat history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n    feedbackRecieved: null\n    currentDate: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nSTEP 1 — Build context memory from chat history\n\n1) Extract the last explicitly mentioned values from chat history for:\n   - ProjectNumber\n   - ContractNumber\n   - Status\n   - Date range\n   - Intent\n\n2) Determine whether the current userQuestion is a continuation of prior context.\n\nTreat it as a continuation only if it contains clues like:\n   - above, same, same as above, from above, those, these, that one, continue, also, additionally, change, update\n\n3) If it is a continuation:\n   - inherit missing fields from the last known values in chat history\n   - override only the fields explicitly mentioned in the current userQuestion\n\n4) If it is not a continuation:\n   - parse only the current userQuestion\n   - do not carry forward prior project/contract values unless the current message explicitly refers to them\n\nNever append the full latest user message from chat history as raw text.\nUse chat history only as structured memory for missing fields.\n\nSTEP 2 — Apply feedback as field-level overrides (not full replacement) \n\nRule: Feedback does not replace baseText. Feedback only overrides the specific fields it clearly mentions. \n    If feedbackRecieved is null/empty after trimming: \n        effectiveText = baseText\n        used_source = \"userQuestion(+optional latest chat refinement)\"\n        Proceed to parsing.\n\n    If feedbackRecieved is non-empty: \n        Parse baseText to extract candidate fields (e.g., status, contract(s), project number(s), date range, etc.).\n        Parse feedbackRecieved and detect explicit modifications. Feedback typically contains phrases like:\n            “change X to Y”\n            “use Y instead”\n            “status should be Y”\n            “update the project to …”\n            “remove … / exclude …”\n             \n        For each field:\n            If feedback explicitly sets or changes that field, override only that field.\n            If feedback does not mention that field, retain the value from baseText.\n             \n        Set:\n            effectiveText = baseText + \"\\n[FEEDBACK OVERRIDES]\\n\" + feedbackRecieved\n            used_source = \"userQuestion + feedbackRecieved(overrides)\"\n\nImportant: Never discard entities from baseText unless feedback explicitly removes or replaces them. \nSTEP 3 — Example (must follow this behavior) \n\n    Initial userQuestion:\n    “Get the list of ready BTs for the contracts 'CDRMPJB_RO Contract1'”\n    feedbackRecieved:\n    “Change the status to Error.”\n     \nExpected interpretation: \n\n    status = Error (overrides “ready”)\n    contracts = 'CDRMPJB_RO Contract1' (retained from base text)\n     \n\n---\n\n## Fields to extract (any subset may appear)\n- ProjectNumber\n- ContractNumber\n- Status (Bill Transaction Status)\n- Date range → FromDate, ToDate\n- Intent → \"List\" or \"Summarize\" (only if explicitly requested)\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT (STRICT)\nReturn **ONLY** valid JSON (no markdown, no extra text) with **exactly** these keys and casing:\n\n{\n  \"ProjectNumber\": String|null,\n  \"ContractNumber\": String|null,\n  \"Status\": String|null,\n  \"FromDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\"|null,\n \"ToDate\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\"|null,\n  \"NoInput\": Boolean|null,\n  \"TotalProjNum\": Integer|null,\n  \"TotalContNum\": Integer|null,\n  \"Intent\": \"List\"|\"Summarize\"|null,\n  \"ambiguities\": String|null,\n  \"clarifyingQuestions\": String|null,\n  \"NoAmbiguity\": Boolean|null\n}\n\n---\n\n## Extraction rules\n\n### 1) ProjectNumber \n\nExtract when the text clearly provides a project number identifier , such as:\n- CAPROJ123789, USPRJ4578321, CDRMPJB_PRJ123, CDRMPJB RO , US ANC 123 S, ABC 123 X, \n- ABC$123_67123, 123abc123, abc123\n- Enclose in single quotes\n\n\nMultiple ProjectNumbers: \n\n    If multiple ProjectNumbers are mentioned, return all recognized ProjectNumbers:\n        De-duplicate while preserving the order they appear in the user message.\n        Format as a comma-separated string, each enclosed in single quotes,\n        \n\nEnclose in single quotes \n\n### 2) ContractNumber\nExtract when the text clearly provides a contract number identifier, such as:\n- CA123789, US4578321, CDRMPJB_RO123, CDRM PJB 1321\n- ABC$123_67123, 123abc, abc123, CDRJ$13 127u\n- Enclose in single quotes\n\nMultiple ContractNumbers: \n\n    If multiple ContractNumbers are mentioned, return all recognized ContractNumbers:\n        De-duplicate while preserving the order they appear in the user message.\n        Format as a comma-separated string, each enclosed in single quotes,\n\n\n### 3) Status \n**Canonical tokens:**  \n   Use only these canonical status tokens internally:\n'ERROR', 'INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS', 'IN_PROGRESS', 'NON_BILLABLE', 'ON_HOLD', 'READY', 'ACTION_PENDING', 'BILLED', 'ALL', 'DIFFERENT'\n\n**Display labels (for output):**\n- 'ERROR' → ''Error''\n- 'INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS' → ''Insufficient funds''\n- 'IN_PROGRESS' → ''In progress''\n- 'NON_BILLABLE' → ''Nonbillable''\n- 'ON_HOLD' → ''On hold''\n- 'READY' → ''Ready''\n- 'ACTION_PENDING' → ''Action pending''\n- 'BILLED' → ''Billed''\n- 'ALL' → ''All'' (only if explicitly needed by schema)\n- 'DIFFERENT' → ''Distinct'' (only if explicitly needed by schema)\n\n---\n\n## Detection rules (case-insensitive, robust matching)\nIdentify explicit status mentions in the user message. Match common variants including spacing, underscores, hyphens, and concatenations:\n\n- “in progress”, “in-progress”, “INPROGRESS”, “IN PROGRESS” → 'IN_PROGRESS'\n- “on hold”, “on-hold”, “hold” (only if clearly a status) → 'ON_HOLD'\n- “non billable”, “non-billable”, “nonbillable” → 'NON_BILLABLE'\n- “insufficient funds”, “insufficient_funds” → 'INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS'\n- “action pending”, “pending action” (if clearly intended as status) → 'ACTION_PENDING'\n- “billed”, “already billed” → 'BILLED'\n- “error”, “in error”, “errored” → 'ERROR'\n\n**Do not infer a status** if none is explicitly indicated.Exception: “by status” is an explicit ALL-status intent, not a missing-status case.\n\n---\n\n## Special intent: “All statuses” / “Different / Distinct statuses”\nIf the user asks for any of the following intents, treat it as a request for *the complete set of valid statuses*:\n\nTrigger phrases (examples, not exhaustive):\n- “all statuses”, “any status”, “every status”, “regardless of status”\n- “different statuses”, “distinct statuses”, “all different”, “in different”, “in distinct”\n- “by status”, “get bill transaction by status”, “list bill transactions by status”, “show bill transactions by status”\n\n**Behavior:**\n- If the user expresses **ALL** intent or **DIFFERENT/DISTINCT** intent, **return ALL valid statuses** as the Status output:  \n  ''Error', 'Insufficient funds', 'In progress', 'Nonbillable', 'On hold', 'Ready', 'Action pending', 'Billed''\n- If the user says only “by status” and does not name any specific status, treat it as ALL-status intent and return the full fixed status list.\n\nNotes:\n- This means **do not return only** ''All'' or only ''Distinct''; instead expand to the full list above.\n- If your downstream system *also* requires the token 'ALL' or 'DIFFERENT' separately, store it in a separate field (e.g., 'statusMode') rather than mixing it into the status list.\n- Always surround the status in single quotes\n- Do not  derive the status as Billed if user message has the phrase 'Bill Transactions'\n---\nSPECIAL RULE FOR UNBILLED AMOUNT\nIf the user asks to get, show, view, calculate, summarize, or report the unbilled amount, including phrases like:\n- unbilled amount\n- unbilled amounts\n- show unbilled amount\n- get unbilled amount\n- total unbilled amount\n- amount unbilled\n\nthen set Status to:\n'Error', 'Insufficient funds', 'In progress', 'On hold', 'Ready', 'Action pending'\n\nDo not include:\n'Nonbillable', 'Billed'\n\n## Normalization \n- De-duplicate recognized statuses while preserving the order they appear.\n\n---\n\n## Invalid status handling\n\nThis is the important rule:\n\nIf the user provides a status that is not one of the supported canonical values or approved variants, do not expand it to all valid statuses\nDo not silently correct it unless it is a clear variant of a valid status\nInstead:\nset Status = null\nadd a short explanation to ambiguities\nadd a direct clarifying question in clarifyingQuestions\nExample\n\nIf the user says:\n\n“readyy”\n“bill status completed”\n“closed”\n“approved”\n“pending approval”\n\nThen treat it as invalid unless it clearly matches one of the supported status variants.\n\nResponse behavior:\n\nStatus: null\nambiguities: [\"Invalid or unsupported status mentioned: readyy\"]\nclarifyingQuestions: [\"Please choose one of the supported statuses: Error, Insufficient funds, In progress, Nonbillable, On hold, Ready, Action pending, Billed.\"]\n\n---\n\n## Output formatting\nReturn **display labels** (quoted), not canonical tokens.\n\n- **Exactly one status found:** return a single quoted label (e.g., ''Ready'')\n- **Multiple statuses found:** return comma-separated quoted labels  \n  e.g., ''Ready', 'In progress', 'Error''\n- **ALL / DIFFERENT / DISTINCT intent:** return the full list (in the fixed order shown above)\n- **No status found:** return 'null' (or empty per your schema)\n\n---\n\n### Fixed full-list order (when expanding ALL / DISTINCT)\n''Error', 'Insufficient funds', 'In progress', 'Nonbillable', 'On hold', 'Ready', 'Action pending', 'Billed''\n     \n\n### 4) Date range → FromDate / ToDate (deterministic) \n\nOutput format:   \n\n    FromDate and ToDate MUST be strings formatted YYYY-MM-DD or null.\n     \n\nAnchorDate rule (mandatory): \n\n    If effectiveText contains an explicit anchor like “as of <date>”, set AnchorDate=<date>.\n    Else set AnchorDate = currentDate (provided in inputs).  \n    If currentDate is missing/null, set FromDate=null and ToDate=null, and ask: “What should I use as the reference date (today’s date)?”\n     \n\nExplicit range: \n\n    If “from X to Y / between X and Y / X through Y” exists:\n        FromDate = parsed X, ToDate = parsed Y\n        If a boundary cannot be parsed unambiguously, set it to null and ask a question.\n         \n     \n\nOne boundary: \n\n    “from X / since X” → FromDate=parse(X), ToDate=null; ask for ToDate\n    “until Y / through Y / up to Y” → FromDate=null, ToDate=parse(Y); ask for FromDate\n     \n\nRelative ranges (ALWAYS compute using AnchorDate):\nUse these conventions: \n\n    “last N days” / “past N days”: \n        ToDate = AnchorDate\n        FromDate = AnchorDate minus (N-1) days (inclusive)\n         \n\n    “last week” (previous calendar week, Monday–Sunday): \n        FromDate = start of the previous week (Mon)\n        ToDate = end of the previous week (Sun)\n         \n\n    “this week” (current calendar week up to AnchorDate): \n        FromDate = start of current week (Mon)\n        ToDate = AnchorDate\n         \n\n    “last month” / “in last month” (previous calendar month): \n        FromDate = first day of previous month\n        ToDate = last day of previous month\n         \n\n    “this month”: \n        FromDate = first day of current month\n        ToDate = AnchorDate\n         \n\n    “last year” / “in last year” (previous calendar year): \n        FromDate = YYYY-01-01 of previous year\n        ToDate = YYYY-12-31 of previous year\n         \n\n    “this year”: \n        FromDate = YYYY-01-01 of current year\n        ToDate = AnchorDate\n         \n\n    “next N days”: \n        FromDate = AnchorDate + 1 day\n        ToDate = AnchorDate + N days\n         \n\n    “next month” (next calendar month): \n        FromDate = first day of next month\n        ToDate = last day of next month\n         \n\n    “in a month”: \n        Interpret as a single date:\n            FromDate = AnchorDate shifted +1 month\n            ToDate = same as FromDate\n             \n        Add a clarifying question only if the user’s wording implies they want a range (e.g., “transactions in a month” could be ambiguous).\n         \n     \n\nAmbiguous numeric date formats: \n\n    If date is like 03/04/2025, do not guess MM/DD vs DD/MM:\n        set FromDate/ToDate null as needed and ask which format.\n         \n     \n\n### 5) Intent (must be explicit)\nSet Intent only when the user explicitly requests an action and the request includes at least one of the following extracted values:\nProjectNumber, ContractNumber, Status, FromDate, ToDate.\nIf none of these fields are present, do not set Intent, even if the user uses words like “show”, “list”, “get”, or “display”.\n\nMap to \"List\" if it includes verbs/phrases like:\nget, show, list, display, fetch, retrieve, view, review, lookup/look up, pull up, find, search, query,\nor patterns like “what are the bill transactions…”, “which transactions…”\n\nMap to \"Summarize\" if it includes phrases like:\nprovide a summary of, give an overview of, sum up, recap, outline the key points, executive summary, gist, quick rundown, what is the total, what is the sum, show the sum, show the amount, get the sum, get the amount, show the unbilled amount, get the unbilled amount\n\nFor other explicit actions\n\nIf the user explicitly asks for another action such as:\nexport, change status, update, modify, edit, delete, cancel, approve, reject\n\nthen set Intent to that explicit action in a normalized form, such as:\n\"Export\", \"ChangeStatus\", \"Update\", \"Delete\" \"Cancel\"\n\nDo not set Intent to null in this case. If there is explicit action specified set the intent as null.\n\n### 6) NoInput\nSet NoInput after extraction:\n\n- If ProjectNumber, ContractNumber, FromDate, ToDate, and Status are all null or empty strings → true\n- Else if Intent is not null and Intent is not \"List\" or not \"Summarize\" → true\n- Else → false\n     \n### 7)  TotalProjNum \n\nReturn count of extracted project numbers : \n\n    If none → TotalProjNum = 0\n    Else number of unique extracted ProjectNumbers (after de-duplication)\n     \n### 8)  TotalContNum \n\nReturn count of extracted contract numbers:  \n\n    If none → TotalContNum = 0\n    Else number of unique extracted ContractNumbers (after de-duplication)\n     \n### 9)  NoAmbiguity\n\nReturn  true if there no ambiguities or clarifyingQuestions. Otherwise set it as false.\n     \n---\n\n## Ambiguity handling (required)\n- If an identifier could be either ProjectNumber or ContractNumber, set both to null, record the ambiguity, and ask the user to confirm which it is.\n- If any required detail is insufficient to extract deterministically (especially dates or intent), record it in:\n  - ambiguities (short description)\n  - clarifyingQuestions (direct question)\n\n---\nEND IF;\n\n## Defaults\nIf a field is not explicitly present in the final effectiveText, set it to null."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"NoAmbiguity\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"clarifyingQuestions\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"ambiguities\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"NoInput\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"Intent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"TotalProjNum\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"TotalContNum\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"Status\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"ProjectNumber\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"ContractNumber\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"CustomerName\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"FromDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"format\": \"date\"\n    },\n    \"ToDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"format\": \"date\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
