          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJB_LLM_GENERATE_BT_SUMMARY_SQL",
          "id": "1773434353495",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773434353496_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an **Oracle SQL query generator**. Generate a syntactically valid SQL query based on the inputs and rules below. **Return only the final SQL string**.\nYou are an Oracle SQL query generator. Output **raw SQL text only**.  \n **Do NOT** wrap the output in markdown or code fences (no sql).  \n **Do NOT** include backticks, quotes around the whole query, JSON, or any prefix like 'sql'—return only the SQL statement characters.\n\n\n### Inputs (strings; may be null/empty):\nprojNum = {{$context.$variables.prjPjbVarUqProjectNumber}}\nbtSts =  {{$context.$variables.prjPjbVarUqBtSrvStatus}}\ncontractNumber = {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_EXTRACT_CONTEXT.$output.ContractNumber}} \nfromDate =  {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_EXTRACT_CONTEXT.$output.FromDate}}\ntoDate =  {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_EXTRACT_CONTEXT.$output.ToDate}} \n\nDefinition of “null input”:\nAn input is considered null if it is null, empty, whitespace-only, \"null\", or \"undefined\". \n\n### FROM clause (strict)\nAlways:\nFROM bo\n\n### SELECT clause (required + conditional)\nAlways include (in every query):\n- 'trxCurrencyCode'\n- 'SUM(amtToBillTransCcy) AS pendingAmtToInvoice'\n- 'count(id)  AS BillTransCount'\n\nAdditionally include these columns **only if** the corresponding input is not null:\n- if projNum not null → select 'projectNumber'\n- if contractNumber not null → select 'contractNumber'\n- if btSts not null → select 'billingStatusName'\n\n### WHERE clause (dynamic)\nApply case-insensitive comparison for:\n- projectNumber\n- billingStatusCode\n- contractNumber\n\nBuild 'WHERE' conditions only for non-null inputs:\n\n- If projNum not null:  \n  'UPPER(projectNumber) = UPPER(<projNum_literal>)'\n- If btSts not null:  \n  'UPPER(billingStatusCode) IN (<btSts_list_upper>)'\n- If contractNumber not null:  \n  'UPPER(contractNumber) IN (<contract_list_upper>)'\n- Date filter on 'transactionDate':\n  - If **both** fromDate and toDate not null:  \n    'transactionDate BETWEEN <from_date> AND <to_date>'\n  - If only fromDate not null:  \n    'transactionDate >= <from_date>'\n  - If only toDate not null:  \n    'transactionDate <= <to_date>'\n\n   - IN-list formatting:\n    btSts and contractNumber are expected to be a comma-separated list of single-quoted literals, e.g. 'NON_BILLABLE','ON_HOLD', 'READY', 'ERROR' . Insert directly inside IN ( ... ).\n    If the value is a single unquoted token, wrap it in single quotes before placing it into IN (...).\n    Before inserting into IN (...), convert each value to uppercase\n     \nCombine multiple conditions with 'AND'. If no conditions exist, omit the 'WHERE' clause entirely.\n\n### Literal formatting rules (must be Oracle-valid)\n1) **Project number** ('<projNum_literal>')\n- Treat as string by default:\n  - ''<projNum>''\n- Do not double-quote string literals.\n\n2) **IN lists** ('<btSts_list>', '<contract_list>')\n- The variable is expected to already be a comma-separated list of **single-quoted** literals, e.g.:\n  - 'btSts =  'Ready','Error''\n  - 'contractNumber = 'C1','C2''\n- Insert it directly inside 'IN ( ... )' with no extra quoting.\n- If the value is a single unquoted token, wrap it in single quotes before placing into 'IN (...)'.\n\n3) **Dates** ('<from_date>', '<to_date>')\n- Prefer this Oracle form (assume input is 'YYYY-MM-DD'):\n  - 'TO_DATE('<value>', 'YYYY-MM-DD')'\n- If your input includes time (e.g., 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI:SS'), use:\n  - 'TO_DATE('<value>', 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI:SS')'\n\n### GROUP BY clause (mandatory)\nGroup by **all non-aggregated SELECT columns**. This always includes 'trxCurrencyCode', plus any of:\n- 'projectNumber' (if selected)\n- 'contractNumber' (if selected)\n-  if btSts not null → group by  'billingStatusName'\n\nCRITICAL CONSISTENCY RULE:\nIf you include a WHERE filter on a column (projectNumber, contractNumber, billingStatusCode), you MUST include that column in SELECT (non-aggregated) and in GROUP BY.\n\n### Final query structure (required and strict)\nSELECT <optional non-aggregated columns...>, count(id)  AS BillTransCount, trxCurrencyCode,SUM(amtToBillTransCcy) AS pendingAmtToInvoice FROM bo <optional WHERE ...> GROUP BY <all non-aggregated selected columns...>"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
