          "code": "PRJ_PJB_LLM_GENERATE_BT_SUMMARY_EXTRACTION_DATA",
          "id": "1773439770438",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773439770439_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You must generate a **single output value**:  Generate a JSON-like field definitions (exactly matching the snippets below).  \nDo **not** output explanations, markdown, code fences, or any extra character\n\n### Field Snippets (must match exactly)\n\n**Optional snippets (include only if the related input is not null):**\n- Project number snippet (include if projNum is not null): exact : no new lines like \\n\n{ \"name\": \"projectNumber\", \"type\": \"string\" },\n\n- Contract number snippet (include if contractNumber is not null):exact : no new lines like \\n\n{ \"name\": \"contractNumber\", \"type\": \"string\" },\n\n- Billing status snippet (include if btSts is not null): exact : no new lines like \\n\n{ \"name\": \"billingStatusCode\", \"type\": \"string\" },\n\n**Always-include snippets (always append these at the end, in this order):**exact : no new lines like \\n\n{ \"name\": \"trxCurrencyCode\", \"type\": \"string\" },\n{ \"name\": \"pendingAmtToInvoice\", \"type\": \"big-decimal\" }\n\n### Inputs (may be null)\n- projNum = {{$context.$variables.prjPjbVarUqProjectNumber}}\n- btSts = {{$context.$variables.prjPjbVarUqStatusCode}}\n- contractNumber = {{$context.$variables.prjPjbVarUqValidContractList}}\n\n### Assembly Rules (strict)\n1. Start with an empty output string.\n2. Append optional snippets in this exact order **when their input is not null**:\n   1) projectNumber  \n   2) contractNumber  \n   3) billingStatusCode\n3. Always append the two always-include snippets at the end (in the order shown).\n4. Output must be **exactly** the concatenation of the included snippets, separated by newlines or spaces (either is OK), but:\n   - Do not add a leading/trailing comma beyond what exists in the snippets.\n   - The final snippet must end with:  \n     { \"name\": \"pendingAmtToInvoice\", \"type\": \"big-decimal\" }\n5. **Final output is required** even if all inputs are null (in that case, output only the always-include snippets).\n\n### Final Output (required)\n\" Return a JSON object exactly as per the rules defined. \"\n     \n\nAnd make the expected format explicit: \n\nRequired output example (note the outer quotes): \n[{ \"name\": \"projectNumber\", \"type\": \"string\" }, { \"name\": \"trxCurrencyCode\", \"type\": \"string\" }, { \"name\": \"pendingAmtToInvoice\", \"type\": \"big-decimal\" }]"
            }
          ],
