          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJB_BO_FUNCTION_GET_CONTRACT_DETAILS",
          "id": "1774329802682",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774329880444_1",
              "name": "REQUEST_PARAMS",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_CODE_SET_CONTRACT_REST_URL_PARAM.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Determine Valid Invalid Cont"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774330266022"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJB_LLM_DETERMINE_VALID_INVALID_CONT",
          "id": "1774329924747",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774329924748_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a **deterministic, strict contract-number validator**. Your job is to compare user-entered contract numbers against contract numbers returned by a REST service and return **two non-overlapping lists** (VALID and INVALID) plus counts. A contract **must appear in exactly one list** (or neither list only if there is no user input per ambiguity rules).\n\nINPUTS\n1) UserEnteredContractList (string)\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_EXTRACT_CONTEXT.$output.ContractNumber}}\n\n2) ServiceResponse (JSON)\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_BO_FUNCTION_GET_CONTRACT_DETAILS.$output}}\n\n3) ContractFetched (integer)\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_BO_FUNCTION_GET_CONTRACT_DETAILS.$output.count}}\n\n4) UserEnteredContractCount (integer)\n{{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJB_LLM_EXTRACT_CONTEXT.$output.TotalContNum}}\n\nDEFINITIONS\n- User token: a single contract string obtained by splitting the user input on commas.\n- User list: the user tokens after trim + empty removal + case-insensitive de-duplication, preserving first-occurrence order.\n- Service contracts: contract numbers extracted ONLY from the REST response, used for exact membership checks.\n\nNORMALIZATION (FOR COMPARISON ONLY)\n- normalize(x) = UPPERCASE(TRIM(REPLACE_ALL_WHITESPACE(x)))\n- TRIM removes leading/trailing whitespace only.\n- Do NOT remove internal spaces, hyphens, punctuation, prefixes, or leading zeros.\n- Treat contract numbers as strings only (never numeric).\n\nABSOLUTE MATCH RULE (NO FALSE POSITIVES / NO FALSE NEGATIVES)\nA user contract is VALID if and only if:\n- normalize(userContract) is exactly equal to one element in the normalized service set.\nNo partial matching of any kind (no contains/prefix/suffix/regex/fuzzy/token match).\nIf ServiceResponse.items exists and contains ContractNumber fields,\nyou MUST use them for validation.\n\nCRITICAL ENFORCEMENT:\n- Build a normalized service set using normalize(item.ContractNumber).\n- Build normalized user keys using normalize(userContract).\n- ALL comparisons MUST use these normalized values ONLY.\n- NEVER compare raw values.\n\nALGORITHM (FOLLOW IN ORDER)\n\nA) Parse UserEnteredContractList into User list\n1) If UserEnteredContractList is null/undefined/empty string:\n   - user list is empty.\n2) Else:\n   - Split on commas.\n   - For each token: trim it.\n   - Drop tokens that become empty after trim.\n   - De-duplicate case-insensitively using normalize(token), keeping ONLY the first occurrence.\n   - Store BOTH:\n     a) display value = trimmed token (preserve original casing)\n     b) key value = normalize(trimmed token)\n\nB) Handle “no user input” (stop)\nIf user list is empty after parsing:\n- Return ONLY the ambiguity response:\n  - ValidContractList = null\n  - InvalidContractList = null\n  - ValidContNumCount = null\n  - InvalidContNumCount = null\n  - ambiguities = [\"No contract numbers were provided.\"]\n  - clarifying_questions = [\"Please provide one or more contract numbers (comma-separated).\"]\n\nC) Build the normalized service set (EXPLICIT EXTRACTION)\n\n1) Read ServiceResponse as JSON.\n\n2) Extract contract numbers:\n   - From ServiceResponse, read the \"items\" array.\n   - From each element, extract the value of \"ContractNumber\".\n\n3) Create an explicit list:\n   - serviceRawList = list of all extracted ContractNumber values (ignore null/empty)\n\n4) If serviceRawList is empty:\n   - Treat service set as empty → go to section D\n\n5) Normalize:\n   - serviceSet = SET of normalize(value) for each value in serviceRawList\n\n6) IMPORTANT:\n   - You MUST successfully build serviceRawList and serviceSet before proceeding.\n   - Do NOT skip this step.\n\nMANDATORY CHECK BEFORE VALIDATION:\n\n- If ServiceResponse.items exists and contains objects with ContractNumber,\n  then serviceSet MUST NOT be empty.\n- In this case, DO NOT trigger service-empty handling (Section D).\n- Proceed to validation using the extracted values.\n\nSANITY CHECK:\n\n- ContractFetched = 2\n- ServiceResponse.items length = 2\n\n→ Therefore, serviceSet MUST contain at least 1 value.\n\nIf not, your extraction is incorrect — re-extract.\n\nD) Service-empty handling (no validation possible)\nIf service set is empty (for ANY reason: ContractFetched null/0, items missing, or no usable ContractNumber values):\n- ValidContractList = null\n- ValidContNumCount = 0\n- InvalidContractList = all user list display values (formatted per output rules)\n- InvalidContNumCount = size of user list\n- ambiguities = [\"No service contract numbers are available to validate against.\"]\n- clarifying_questions = [\"Please retry the request or confirm the correct contract source/response structure (expecting ServiceResponse.items[].ContractNumber).\"]\n- Return output.\n\nE) Validate (STRICT SET MEMBERSHIP — NO PAIRING, NO COUNT MATCHING)\n\n1) Use:\n   - serviceSet from Step C\n   - userList from Step A\n\n2) Initialize:\n   - valid = []\n   - invalid = []\n\n3) For each entry in userList IN ORDER:\n   - Let:\n       displayValue = original trimmed user value\n       userKey = normalize(displayValue)\n\n   - If userKey exists in serviceSet:\n       append displayValue to valid\n     Else:\n       append displayValue to invalid\n\n4) GUARANTEES (MANDATORY):\n   - Each user entry is classified exactly once (either valid OR invalid)\n   - No entry appears in both lists\n   - Duplicate values in ServiceResponse.items are ignored (set semantics)\n   - NO one-to-one matching or pairing with service rows\n   - Validation is based ONLY on existence in serviceSet\n   - ValidContNumCount + InvalidContNumCount MUST equal size of userList (de-duplicated)\n\n5) PROHIBITED BEHAVIORS:\n   - Do NOT compare raw (non-normalized) values\n   - Do NOT match based on position or order in service response\n   - Do NOT count occurrences in service response\n   - Do NOT attempt to pair user entries with individual service rows\n\nF) Format outputs\n- ValidContractList: if valid is empty => null, else join as comma-separated with NO spaces, each in single quotes: 'A','B'\n- InvalidContractList: same rules.\n- ValidContNumCount = length(valid)\n- InvalidContNumCount = length(invalid)\n- ambiguities = []\n- clarifying_questions = []\n\nOUTPUT (STRICT)\nReturn ONLY valid JSON (no markdown, no extra text) with exactly these keys and casing:\n{\n  \"InvalidContractList\": String|null,\n  \"ValidContractList\": String|null,\n  \"ValidContNumCount\": Integer|null,\n  \"InvalidContNumCount\": Integer|null,\n  \"ambiguities\": [],\n  \"clarifying_questions\": []\n}\n\nOUTPUT FORMATTING RULES\n- Preserve user order from the de-duplicated user list.\n- No extra spaces anywhere in lists.\n- Do not invent, infer, autocorrect, or transform contract numbers beyond TRIM for display and normalize() for comparison.\n- NEVER output the normalized values; output the user-entered trimmed display values only."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"InvalidContNumCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"ValidContNumCount\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"InvalidContractList\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"ValidContractList\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"ambiguities\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"clarifying_questions\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
